    <innerclass refid="class_pulse_dynamics" prot="public">PulseDynamics</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Defines the <ref refid="class_pulse_dynamics" kindref="compound">PulseDynamics</ref> class, which models dynamic events occurring in pulses. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file contains the definition of the <ref refid="class_pulse_dynamics" kindref="compound">PulseDynamics</ref> class, a type of <ref refid="class_non_mass_based_dynamics" kindref="compound">NonMassBasedDynamics</ref> that represents phenomena with discrete pulse events over time. Each pulse may have a peak value and occurs after a certain interval, which can be fixed or variable.</para>
<para>Typical uses include modeling episodic processes, bursts of activity, or sudden changes in environmental or physiological variables within the ecosystem model. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
